My estimate of fair value is about 9.5. Before the first trade it was 10.5, the mean of three dice. The counterparty selling to me at 7 is mild evidence of a low sum, because an informed seller would only sell if the sum was below 7. That moves the estimate down from 10.5 to roughly 9.5.

I'm long one unit, so I shade the quotes to favour selling. The spread is wide enough to cover the 35% chance of facing an informed counterparty.

