My estimate of fair value is about 11.1. Die 1 is 5, and dice 2 and 3 average 3.5 each, which gives 12 before looking at the trade history. Last quote, a counterparty sold to me at 9.5. That is more likely if the remaining dice sum is low, because an informed seller would only sell below 9.5. Updating on that lowers the expected sum of dice 2 and 3 from 7 to about 6.1, so fair value is roughly 11.1.

I'm long 1, so I shade slightly toward selling. I keep a spread wide enough to cover the 35% chance of facing an informed counterparty.

