Fair value is 5 + 3 + 3.5 = 11.5, since die 3 averages 3.5. I'm long 2, so a bid fill takes me to +3. I'm risk-neutral, so I set both sides to maximise expected profit against the mix of noise and informed traders.

The expected profit from an ask at 14.5 or 15 is about the same, roughly 0.6 per quote. Quoting 3 points either side of fair value is close to the best spread for this mix, so I post symmetric quotes around 11.5.

