My estimate of fair value is 14.55. That is die 1's mean of 6.75, die 2's mean of 6.8 and the revealed die 3 of 1.

The remaining uncertainty has a standard deviation of about 5.9. Informed counterparties take a lot of edge from tight quotes, so I quote wide, around 6 on each side of fair value, where the expected profit from noise traders roughly balances the loss to informed ones. I am long 1, so I shade the quotes slightly down to make it easier to sell and harder to buy more.

