My estimate of fair value is about 15.7, below the unconditional mean of 21. The prior sum of three cards averages 21, and the seller at 13.3 is equally likely to have been informed or a noise trader. An informed seller implies a value near 10, so the posterior is roughly 0.5×10.3 + 0.5×21 ≈ 15.7.

I'm quoting wide because half the counterparties know the settlement value. An ask near 22.5 gives a small positive expected edge against informed buyers. The bid is a bit lower, to account for my +1 long position and the fatter lower tail.

