Most of my profit comes from noise traders. Informed traders cost me less the further my quotes sit from fair value. Working through the numbers, the expected edge per side is small at tight spreads and levels off at roughly 8 to 9 away from fair value. I'm long +2, so I keep the bid slightly wide and bring the ask in a little to make selling more likely.

