Before any cards are revealed, the settlement value (the sum of 3 cards) has mean about 23.8 and standard deviation about 9.4. The deck's total is 119 over 15 cards, so each card averages 7.93, and the sum of three averages 23.8. The variance per card is about 34.2, and sampling without replacement scales the three-card variance to about 88.

A narrow spread loses money to informed counterparties, who trade only when I am off by more than my edge. At a half-spread of about 3 the expected loss to informed traders is about 1.2 per side, against only about 0.5 gained from noise traders. Noise-trader gains and informed losses roughly balance at a half-spread of about 8. The edge turns slightly positive at about 10. I'm quoting about 10 either side of 23.8.

