Fair value is the expected sum of three cards, 3 × 119/15 ≈ 23.8. The standard deviation of the sum is about 9.4.

Against a 50% informed counterparty, a narrow spread loses money. The informed side takes more from me than the noise side pays. The spread only breaks even at a half-width of roughly 8, and it earns a small positive edge from about 10 to 12. I'll quote about 11 either side of 23.8.

