Card 1 is 0, so the remaining 14 cards hold 3 zeros, 2 fours, 3 nines, 1 twelve, 3 fourteens and 2 fifteens. That averages 8.5 per card, so the two unseen cards sum to about 17.0 in expectation, with a standard deviation near 7.7.

Half the counterparties are informed and trade only when I'm wrong, so I need a wide spread. Under a normal approximation, my expected profit per quote is highest at roughly 9–10 either side of 17. I'm quoting 9 on each side.

