Card 3 comes from the 11 remaining cards: four 2s, three 10s, three 13s and one 14. The settlement value is 27 plus card 3, so it is 29, 37, 40 or 41. The expected value is about 35.27.

Only the bid is allowed this quote because I'm at -3. Any bid at or below 29 is never hit by the informed trader, since their value is at least 29. Above 29, the informed trader sells to me whenever card 3 is a 2, which has probability 4/11. That costs me about 0.36 per point of bid above 29, which outweighs the extra noise-trader edge. So the best bid is about 29, and I'll post 28.9 to stay clear of a tie.

