The sum of two cards drawn from this deck has a mean of 16.5 and a standard deviation of about 4.1. The 16 cards total 132, so each card averages 8.25 and the pair averages 16.5. The per-card variance is about 8.94, and the without-replacement correction gives a pair variance of about 16.7.

Half of the counterparties are informed and know the settlement value, so a tight spread loses money to them. I modelled the settlement value as roughly normal and compared each side's expected profit from noise traders against its expected loss to informed ones. That profit is maximised at a half-spread of about 1.25 standard deviations, or roughly 5.1. Centred on 16.5, that puts the bid near 11.4 and the ask near 21.6.

