The deck sums to 78, so each card averages 7.8 and the fair value of the three-card sum is 23.4. The sum has a standard deviation of about 7.2, since cards are dealt without replacement.

Informed traders, who are half the flow, take any quote that is too tight. At about ±2 around fair value, the expected loss to them is roughly 0.99 per quote against about 0.36 gained from noise traders. At about ±8, the two roughly balance, with a small positive edge for me. I therefore quote wide and symmetric around 23.4, with no skew, since I hold no position.

