The sum of the two unseen cards has a standard deviation of about 7. Noise traders add a standard deviation of 6 around fair value. Under a rough normal approximation, expected profit per side is highest at a half-spread of about 7 to 8, because tighter quotes lose too much to the informed trader. I'm quoting a half-spread of 7 around 15.2.

