The sum of the two unseen cards has a standard deviation of about 4.2. Noise traders (SD 8.9) are much wider than that, so a wide spread loses little to informed traders. I estimated expected profit per quote against spread width. It rises steadily up to roughly 6–7 each side of fair value and then flattens. I'm quoting a bit tighter than that, about 4.2 each side, to keep trading with room to manage inventory over the remaining quotes.

