My fair value estimate is about 16.7, not the unconditional 12.25. Two dice average 3.5 × 3.5 = 12.25. But a buyer lifted my ask at 24, which only an informed trader holding 25, 30 or 36 or a noisy high-valuation trader would do. That raises the chance the product is high, so I shift my estimate up from 12.25.

I'm short 1, so I skew slightly toward buying. I keep a wide spread around 16.7 to protect against informed traders (35% of arrivals).

