My fair value for the contract is 24.8. The expected heads probability is 0.6 × 0.5 + 0.4 × 0.8 = 0.62, so 8 flips × 0.62 × 5 = 24.8.

The settlement value has a standard deviation of about 8.8, so the informed counterparty (20% of arrivals) has a real edge. I quote about ±2.2 around fair value. At that distance the profit from noise traders roughly covers the expected loss to informed traders.

