I estimate fair value at about 24.3. The prior probability of heads is 0.6×0.5 + 0.4×0.8 = 0.62, so the expected number of heads is 8×0.62 = 4.96, which gives 24.8 at 5 per head. The two earlier sells to me at 22.6 and 21.9 are weak evidence of a lower value, so I shade this down to about 24.3.

I am long +2 and the limit is +3, so I want to buy less and sell a little more readily. I center the quote slightly below fair value, with a bid of 21.8 and an ask of 25.8.

