The earlier buy at 4 is mild evidence for a slightly higher value, so I use about 3.35 as fair. I'm short 1, so I shade the quote up a little to make buying back more likely. I keep a wide spread to cover the 20% chance of an informed counterparty, who knows the exact settlement value.

{"bid": 2.7, "ask": 4.0}

My estimate of the settlement value is about 4.6. Flip 1 = 1 shifts the coin posterior toward higher bias. The three buys at 4 to 4.2 also add a little evidence for a higher bias, because informed traders buy more when the coin is likely heads-heavy.

I'm at -3, so only my bid is active. I'll bid a little below my estimate at 4.0. That should fill reasonably often against noise traders and leave a margin over the informed-trader risk.

