The three revealed flips (heads, heads, tails) shift the coin posterior to roughly 9% for p = 0.2, 48% for p = 0.5 and 43% for p = 0.7. That gives E[p] ≈ 0.557. With 2 heads already in and 4 flips still to come, the fair value is about 2 + 4 × 0.557 ≈ 4.23.

I'm short 3, so only the bid is allowed. Buying below fair value is profitable in expectation and also reduces my short exposure. A bid of 3.9 sits about 0.3 under fair value. That keeps a good chance of a noise-trader fill while limiting the loss when an informed seller knows the value is low.

