My position is -3, so I can only quote a bid. I compared expected profit across bid levels, counting noise traders selling to me and informed traders selling when the value is 3. Expected profit per quote rises as the bid falls from 4.0 to about 2.2, then flattens. Buying also frees up my ask for the remaining quotes, and the ask side has positive edge too. That favours a higher bid than the pure per-quote optimum, so I'll bid 3.0.

